    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d329-a2">

                <pb facs="0562" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg462"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    118.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prince Devawongsa to Mr. Halderman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pivate
                            Secretary’s Office</hi>, <placeName><placeName type="venue"><hi
                                    rendition="#small-caps">Grand Palace</hi></placeName>, <lb/>
                            <placeName type="city"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bangkok</hi></placeName></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 14,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Ministre</hi>: I have the honor to
                    inclose for your excellency’s information a copy of the dispatch received this
                    day from his royal highness Somdetch Krom Phra Bamrap, the minister of the
                    interior of the North to his royal highness Krom Man Bijit Prejakorn, the
                    special commissioner for the western Laos States, under the date of the 9th
                    August, in reference to the establishment of the missionary school, hospital,
                    &amp;c., at the Nakhon Lampang, or generally called Lakhon, one of the
                    northwestern Laos States, in terms of the application of Mr. McGilvary, made
                    through your excellency.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DEVAWONGSA VAROPRAKAR.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
